User: Cool, that was interesting. So, we have a right triangle where one leg is $\text{100 + 10t}\,$ feet, the other is 100 feet, and the hypotenuse is 110 feet. By the Pythagorean Theorem,\begin{align*} (100 + 10t)^2 + 100^2 &= 110^2\\ 10000 + 2000t + 100t^2 + 10000 &= 12100\\ 100t^2 + 2000t - 2100 &= 0\\ t^2 + 20t - 21 &= 0. \end{align*}So $t = \frac{-20\pm\sqrt{20^2 - 4(-21)}}{2} = -10\pm\sqrt{121}.$ Since $t\,$ is the time it takes for people to walk, we take the positive answer. So $t = 1.$</answer>
